{
  "_readme": [
    "Themes for ghost builds. Each palette role is an ARRAY of block ids; first entry = dominant use, later entries = variation/texture blocks of the same family.",
    "Use ratio ~60% primary / 30% secondary / 10% accent. trim = frame lines (corners, beams, floor/ceiling edge). detail = small props. light = emitters (hide them, see principles.md L-rules).",
    "'shapes' lists the stairs/slab/wall that match primary or secondary, so you can add depth. Any vanilla full block can usually take _stairs/_slab/_wall suffix, check availability first.",
    "Ids with [state] = write exactly like that in the ghost. Plain id = default state.",
    "AE2 CABLES, TERMINALS, BUSES AND MONITORS ARE PARTS ON ae2:cable_bus, NOT BLOCKS. Do not put them in ghosts. Use placeholders (see multiblocks.md)."
  ],
